{"kind":"assert","text":"Cutover head (05d618e2), addendum to da1a7606: question 9 and one scope check.\n\nQuestion 9. Two stand-in membership references outside tests still build { scope, inc, kind }. One is reference(kind) at cli/src/application-scenarios.ts:33, for the scripted test grants. The other is scopeReference(kind) at define/src/story.ts:61, for story actors. Each needs a genesis. I recommend that both call scriptedSequence(seed, time, 2).at. For define, that needs choice (a) of question 8, because define does not depend on scope. The other options are a stand-in digest, which ruling 5 forbids, or the scope's own address, which names the wrong scope. I hold both until question 8 is answered.\n\nScope check on ruling 7 of 862eb586. Commit c6c836b5 applies the same treatment to the other platform readers that compared a stored reference's kind: about 20 files. Their isScopeRef, isFactRef, same and scope-ID checks stay, and the kind comparison goes. Four cohort and register checks now read input.sourceKind !== \"directory\". A field-declaration check such as field.kind !== \"destination\" describes the schema, so it stays. If you want ruling 7 limited to the four sites it named, I revert c6c836b5.\n\nStatus. packages/platform/src no longer reads inc. Main is merged into the branch as c02c45c6. The first compile runs after the NF-2 gate."}